READY TO DEPLOY (merged into development, not on the server yet; dev1 deploys)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- dev2, PR #921 (#908): core only, no migration or setting. A campaign's DM can look up a
  spell, a condition or a creature in the free rules (SRD), privately. Slash commands
  re-sync when core restarts. Check, 2 minutes, on the test server as a DM: press
  **Settings** on the DM screen, then **Look up a rule**; type Fireball (a card: name, level
  and range line, the text, "Source: SRD 5.2.1, Spell Descriptions, p. 131"); again with
  Goblin (it says "Goblin is now called Goblin Warrior in the newer rules"); again with
  Grappled (a condition card, no facts line); again with a made-up word (it says it couldn't
  find it in the free rules, and offers close names to press, none picked for you). Try
  `/dmbot rule name:` and type "fire": names open as you type. If a house rule names the
  thing, it shows first as "House rule N". As a player (not a DM) `/dmbot rule name:Fireball`
  says only a campaign's DM can look up rules. Nothing appears in the channel or the
  transcript. Core logs no ERROR.
- #925 (follow-ups to #914's counts): ears AND core together, no migration. Check with
  DMBOT_DEBUG_AUDIO=1: nothing new on the DM screen; `Capture check:` says "1 decode error"
  (singular); the counts in `audio user=` lines are as before. No separate test needed.

